Lojbab:
> The discursives are among other things intended to be used for
> naturalistic short forms for regular logical apparatus.

I'm not sure we really need them. At least the case for short forms
ought to be really strong. Yes, to figure out the logic of something
first time is really hard, but once that's been done we can start to
get familiar with it. And I don't think this process of familiarization
necessarily requires short forms; it just needs practice.

Also, it seems a potentially confusing syntax-semntics mismatch to mix up
discursives with logical stuff.

